WEBVTT

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.430
Nothing but the same anime,
day in day out.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.890
It's like he has no emotions whatsoever.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.020
It sometimes feels like he doesn't even
recognize me as his mother.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.150
That cut on his forehead
will probably leave a scar.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.700
His father does nothing
to help me at all.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.820
He says he's on a business trip today too.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.290
But I know that's a lie.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.790
He's not on any business trip.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.750
To make matters worse,
Satoru just sits watching the same anime.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.500
His father puts all the blame on me.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.670
He thinks it's my fault that
our son was born this way.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.930
I suppose that's why he spites me
by having affairs.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:00.430
I know.
 I'll just have to get my own back...

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.430
I'll get back at him...

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.350
by committing suicide!

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.150
Satoru!

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.320
Stop it, Satoru!

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:20.660
What are you doing?
Why do you always do this...?

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:24.870
Why? Why does he behave like that, doctor?

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.210
I can't stop thinking I should
just have him committed...

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.090
These hospitals are always so dreary...

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.220
No smoking in the hospital!

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.560
Please go find a smoking area!

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.270
Mind your own business, sausage legs!

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.940
I'm obviously smoking by the toilet
because I couldn't find the smoking area!

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.480
Mr. Katsuragi, no smoking in the hospital.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:55.940
Hayashi!

00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:00.530
If you hurried the hell up,
I wouldn't have some woman bothering me!

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.910
I was out in the car park looking for you.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.250
Shut it!

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:09.750
And don't even think about showing me
your endoscopy trick.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.500
Mr. Katsuragi.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.510
I think that kid might be one.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.510
You can tell?

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.640
Maybe.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.640
I was like that as a kid too.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.400
Oh no, looks like I got
 the wrong return time.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.910
I can't take much more...

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:47.160
Enough! Why am I the only one to suffer?
You always take it out on me...

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.370
Hey. How's it going?

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.040
This place doesn't seem like much fun.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:55.050
Who are you, mister?

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.800
I'm a bit like Matasaburo,
the wind spirit.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.340
Matasa...?

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:04.220
Right... I guess you're too young
to know that story.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.930
So, this is all your mom's
inner turmoil, is it?

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.940
You sure visit some scary places.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.690
Is that why you always sit so still?

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.570
Yeah.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:22.070
You visit these scary places because
the portal to your heart is always open.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:23.450
Portal?

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.580
A portal's like a door.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.450
It can be opened and closed.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.620
You mean the Everywhere Door?

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.710
The Everywhere Door?

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.630
That there.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.630
Huh... pretty impressive, kid.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.050
Why d'you say that?

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:45.140
Using an "image" like that
is something not everybody can do.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:51.310
Now, let's use this door to go to
your favorite place in the world.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.730
My favorite place in the world...?

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.230
Ah, right...

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.900
You don't have
any memories of your own yet.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:05.570
Let's try it this way then. I'll share
a place from my memories with you.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.950
Okay, let's open the door together.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:11.580
Here we go.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:30.140
This is the place in my memories
I like the most.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:34.940
Mr. Matasa, this place isn't scary at all.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.440
Doesn't the wind feel great?

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.190
The wind can travel anywhere.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:43.820
Anywhere?

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.950
That's right.
The wind taught me something.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.040
That I have the power
to freely shape my future.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.870
The ability to mold it as I choose.
An ability called an "image".

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.750
Let's make this place your "peak".

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.250
My peak?

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:02.880
So...

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.720
The place that holds
your most treasured memories.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:12.220
Any bad memories, you should put away
in another place, your "valley".

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:15.770
If you make a "peak" and a "valley"
like that,

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.520
you can live a normal life,
the same as everyone else.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.480
Now, listen closely.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:25.110
This is the most important thing of all.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:31.160
Keep your peak and your valley
closed to all others.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.160
Don't let anyone touch or alter them
in any way.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:40.090
IN THE LANDSCAPE OF THE HUMAN MEMORY,
"THEY" GAVE NAMES TO JUST TWO LOCI,

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.880
"PEAKS" AND "VALLEYS".

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.850
THE CRUSHERS

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:18.430
Say, Tsukasa.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.600
What do you say we open up
a bar, down the line?

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.900
I bet it'd be a lot of fun.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:27.280
Somewhere like this dingy drinking hole.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:28.940
Dingy is it?

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.740
Sure, but I'll be the manager.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:32.990
Says who?

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.450
In that case, I get to be the director.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.240
Check it out, fireworks!

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.660
Or should I say, waterworks!

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.880
What're you doing, dumbass!

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.840
You're getting everything wet!

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.340
-I told you to put the parasol away first!
-You ain't scary from up there, man.

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:52.550
Hey, I heard that, Hiroki!

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.510
Kenji's hearing is incredible...

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.770
Dammit. Now it's going to get all moldy.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.190
Hey. Go get changed, you two.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:11.400
What's it to you? We'll just dry off.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.950
Who do you think our customers are?

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:17.740
I ain't running a gay bar here,
so enough with the wet t-shirts.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:20.040
Watch the wandering hands, you perv!

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.210
Let's go get changed, Hiroki.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.580
I'm calling sexual harassment.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.340
Gimme a break.

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:35.300
Hey. Those two who went up to
the second floor,

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:37.100
are they related to Yokota?

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.970
Yokota? He left this place a while back.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:41.220
Oh?

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:44.190
One day he just came out with
"I'm headed for Bali."

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.350
He's not coming back for 2 or 3 years.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:49.270
So I decided to rent that floor out
to someone else.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:52.190
And after all the years
we'd worked together...

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:57.700
Still, the idea of not having orders
barked at me gives me a sense of relief.

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:01.080
Yet I detect a tinge of melancholy.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:02.910
Nah.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.750
I'm just bored 'cause I've got no one
to argue with anymore.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.840
But I've got these two lively
idiots with me now, so...

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.130
I figured I'd put them to work in the bar.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:14.880
Thanks, but I'm not smoking these days.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:20.140
Just tell me you're not subbing
any of my jobs to them. Are you?

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.810
Don't sweat it, man.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:25.890
I can handle the work you give me
just fine on my own.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.400
Glad to hear it.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.900
By the way, Kenji,

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.400
you got the keys to your van?

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:36.860
Yeah, sure.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:39.780
I'm swapping cars with you for a while.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.080
I'll tell you where to go, tonight.

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:44.540
I'll leave your van at the spot.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:49.540
Put the item you pick up in the trunk of
this car. Leave the spare key behind too.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:52.550
You know how the rest goes.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:55.420
Don't go asking too many questions, right?

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:56.670
Don't worry.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:10:01.680
I didn't even ask my best friend
why he took off for Bali.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.700
Dammit, man!

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.210
This is too much for one guy.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:31.460
Yokota, you pain in the ass,

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:34.630
leaving me to do all the heavy lifting.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.260
We'd split everything
down the middle until now.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.970
Job done, I guess.

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:56.650
Shit!

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.820
The job ain't done at all!

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:10.920
Mr. Katsuragi,
there's no spare key in here.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:18.380
Crap, this is bad.
There's someone there.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:27.720
Tell me that's not the cops.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.390
Get a move on.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.020
The sun'll be up soon.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.810
Phew, it's Mr. Katsuragi.

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:34.730
Mr. Ka...

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:40.110
Something wrong?

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.530
No. Just my imagination.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:45.070
What the hell?

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.870
Aren't you supposed to be in Bali, Yokota?

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:58.300
-What speed you doing now, then?
-100 miles an hour!

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:01.880
Hey... what the hell's
 going on here, Yokota?

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:05.220
How d'you fancy taking to the skies?

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:06.100
Yeah!

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:09.310
If you head back the way we came,
there's a tunnel.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.020
Hit the accelerator
as soon as you leave it.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:15.060
Do that and you'll touch the sky.

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:16.060
What?

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:19.690
-Look at that, it's time to go.
-Yeah!

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:23.570
Steam train! Steam train! All aboard!

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:27.030
Here we go! Choo-choo!

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:28.160
Crap!

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:32.000
Yokota...

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:33.580
Yokota.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:36.420
Yokota. Yokota. Yokota.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:38.250
Yokota!

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:55.440
Kenji. You really don't remember?

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:59.440
We both saw it when we were
retrieving those counterfeit bills.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.280
What were you on about?

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:02.940
Counterfeit bills?

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:06.990
What's going on here...?

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:19.880
What happened to that spare key?

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:24.720
Hey, you listening over there?
 The spare key...

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:26.880
I told you to leave it behind.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:29.640
What? You forgot?

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:32.020
You really are useless.

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:36.390
Fine. Let's meet at the usual park.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:42.530
I really am not a morning person.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:46.150
The dew reminds me of
school girls' sweaty gym socks.

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:55.790
This is your payment.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:58.920
Go wipe your ass with it!

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.790
Whoa. No need to be so rude.

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.920
I've hidden the key in a safe place.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:08.680
If anything happens to me,
it goes straight to the police.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:12.930
What're you laughing at?

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:17.390
You just reminded me of another guy who
said the very same thing not long ago.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.480
Turned out he wasn't even bluffing,

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:22.320
and the key actually did get sent
to the police.

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:26.440
That bastard Yokota gave me
a bunch of extra work.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:32.200
Besides, who wants to work with
someone with no sense of humor?

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.490
You murderer!

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:38.160
I'm not interested in what you think
but I do want that key of yours.

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:39.790
You've got it on you, right?

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:46.090
Hurtling off the road like that,
he'd clearly lost his mind.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:49.300
Just what did you assholes do to him?

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.470
You were bluffing when
you said you'd quit too.

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:01.400
I know you really want a smoke.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.400
I see right through you.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:10.990
Now, I guess...

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:14.280
it's just a matter of getting
the information from you.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:18.500
I've called in the crushers.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:20.290
I'd watch my back if I were you.

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:30.090
The "crushers"?

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:35.510
Really, Kaori? Your family owns a yacht?

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:36.850
Very cool.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:38.850
When's that, then?

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:40.600
Hey!

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:45.730
What's that face for?

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.610
What about your face
when you're talking to Kaori?

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:52.320
It's her fault we're working so late
the morning paper's already come.

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.490
She's an important client.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:58.660
Children should keep quiet
when the adults are talking.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:00.960
Who you calling a child?

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.960
You, because you are!

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.750
Save the foreplay for after breakfast!

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:07.550
We're having a fight...

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.050
Whatever. Cut it out!

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:13.050
Hey man, you can't just
walk in as you please.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:14.260
Listen, you two.

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:18.510
How d'you both like the sound
of managing the bar?

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:23.900
I know it's sudden, but I was thinking
of checking out Bali for 2 or 3 years.

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:25.940
You guys wanted to run a bar, right?

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.400
He who runs away,
 lives to fight another day.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.360
It's all the bosses' fault.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:34.910
Sinking those fake bills right next to
that body encased in concrete...

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:37.990
Kenji and Yokota were bound to see it!

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:41.120
Their faces were white as sheets
when they came up.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:46.540
Of course, the bosses think
sorting such a mess is easy.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:51.260
"Just make them forget everything,"
they said.

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:56.180
How about a bit more of
a head's up next time?

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:00.060
Then I end up with Yokota pretending
he didn't see anything

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:04.060
and Kenji really believing
he didn't see anything.

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:06.850
Of course Yokota's going to wonder
what the hell's up!

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:15.200
Makes sense that he'd steal
a banknote or two to protect himself.

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:16.450
Well...

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:20.580
I think you've done pretty well
considering you don't use an image.

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:21.830
Satoru.

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:25.160
If you've got something to say,
don't mince your words.

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:30.550
If you just transfer the rent money,

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:33.460
you boys can keep
whatever profits are made.

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:35.470
I'll do it! I'll totally do it!

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:37.640
How much is the rent anyway?

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:40.100
I'll send more details when I get there.

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:42.850
Just make sure you tell
people that I'm in Bali.

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:47.140
When really I'll be in LA,
far away from Bali!

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:49.810
Anyway, I'd better get going.

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:54.110
Huh? This is addressed to me...

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:58.410
That was on the floor
when the newspaper came in.

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:00.070
On the floor?

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:03.740
I even went up to the 3rd floor to give it
to you but you weren't in.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:05.620
AIRPLANE TICKET TO LA,
NOT BALI

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:08.620
KAORI

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.880
Weird... I thought I broke it.

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:16.090
It's Kaori.

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:17.380
Hello?

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:21.680
Sorry about that, my smartphone's
on the fritz at the moment.

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:24.810
She hung up...

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:27.560
Gimme. I'll take a look for you.

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:29.400
You saying you can fix it?

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:31.310
Is there something wrong?

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:33.190
You're really sweating

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:34.780
and acting a bit weird.

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:36.150
Weird...?

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:40.740
You two are the weird ones here!
What the hell're you doing?

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:43.240
I'm repairing his phone.
What does it look like?

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:45.370
Are you alright?

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:47.410
Huh?

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:49.170
What's up with you?

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:51.170
You're looking kind of pale.

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:52.710
Yeah...

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.920
Weird...

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:58.220
I must be tired.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:01.680
Man, my head hurts.

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:04.560
I'm just grabbing some water.

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:06.180
You got a headache?

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.560
This is the best cure for a headache.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:09.810
What the...!

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:17.570
Hey.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:30.620
What's that doing there?

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:32.920
I'm supposed...

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:35.250
to have quit.

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:38.420
Quit messing with me!

00:19:40.420 --> 00:19:43.140
What're you doing, man?
You're gonna hurt somebody!

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:44.720
You're losing it, dude!

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:47.680
That's it...

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.850
It was Katsuragi!
He did something to me!

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:54.360
There you go again.

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:56.110
You don't get it! Listen to me!

00:19:56.440 --> 00:20:00.070
He knows some guys who can
get inside people's heads!

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:03.410
Those freaks know how
to bend people to their will!

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:05.490
I'm telling you, it's true!

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:07.490
They made Yokota drive off a cliff!

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.410
I saw it with my own eyes!
You gotta believe me.

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:14.080
Would I be acting this nuts,
if it wasn't true?

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:17.420
Don't worry.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:19.760
We believe you.

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:24.090
No...

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:25.390
Are you two...

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:27.510
the crushers?

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:33.020
I knew something fishy was going on.

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:37.520
Out of the blue, the guy's off to Bali.
I mean, who does that?

00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:41.610
But I never would've guessed
Yokota was a murderer.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:46.030
Then again, it doesn't surprise me
all that much to be honest.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:51.540
The guy lived like he'd given up hope
long ago.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:55.170
I knew he'd meet a bad end
one way or another.

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:00.670
Pretty awful guy, that Yokota.

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:02.720
I'm sure he was a pain in your ass too.

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:07.090
You've got that right! I even got taken in
for questioning 'cause of him!

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:10.850
But don't worry about a thing.

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:15.190
I didn't mention anything
about our dealings.

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:18.810
I'm not the slightest bit
concerned about that.

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:22.860
Oh hey. You're back.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:26.820
Who do we have here? Relatives of yours?

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:29.200
Nah, nothing like that.

00:21:29.780 --> 00:21:32.950
I've been renting Yokota's room
to these two.

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:36.000
Did you finish packing your things?

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:37.210
Yes.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:40.340
We took the liberty of
using the furniture.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:42.340
Thanks for having us.

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:46.590
Well, I guess no one wants to stay
in a murderer's room.

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:50.350
Yokota taking off like that
caused you boys some problems, too.

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:53.970
Hopefully this will
make up for your troubles.

00:21:54.310 --> 00:21:55.520
No need.

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:56.730
Huh?

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:59.360
Keep it for cigarette money.

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:02.780
What? Seriously?

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:04.610
Lucky me!

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:07.200
Goodbye, then.

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:55.010
Artist: Ranjo Miyake
